   "source_line": "| Decode (sparkDash, thinking off) | **DFlash** code 69.8 / prose 25.8 at 1 stream (190.3 / 103.0 agg at 8). **EAGLE MTP** code 46.0 / prose 35.0 (138.7 / 119.9 at 8) | ; | Prefill | peak **2,558 tok/s** at 8K, 1,227 at 128K, 764 at 256K (sparkDash). Chunk size not yet laddered |"
  },
  "notes": "Default variant. Experts are native MXFP4 (U8 nibbles + E8M0 scales), rest of checkpoint FP8 block-quant; needs SGLang with sgl-project/sglang#40448 (nightly 20260921+) or experts expand to FP8 (~151 GiB/rank) and crash the Spark. Args are what boot.py builds from .env.example (the .env written on first run); sglang is launched as python -m sglang.launch_server by boot.py (API_KEY env adds --api-key). Decode CUDA graphs must be off under EAGLE multi-layer (capture crashes). MEM_FRACTION_STATIC 0.93 is deliberately aggressive; boot.py kills sglang if MemAvailable < MEM_GUARD_GIB. start.sh built-in defaults differ from .env.example (e.g. CONTEXT_LENGTH 262144, MEM_FRACTION 0.85, chunked prefill 32768); .env.example values are the documented config. ~82.7 GiB resident weights per rank; weight load 96 s/rank. Multimodal: text, image, video, audio.",
